UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Institut Teknologi Bandung - ''ITB Presidential Scholarship for International Students'' is an invented importer name; ITB''s international awards are the Ganesha Talent Fellowship and the national KNB scheme (retired)', description = 'RETIRED in Pass 124 (2026-10-28) as an invented importer name. There is no "ITB Presidential Scholarship for International Students". ITB''s official Directorate of Partnerships scholarships page, fetched first-hand for this pass, lists exactly four inbound scholarship programmes for international students: (1) the Ganesha Talent-International Fellowship (GT-IF) - ITB-funded, for master and doctoral programmes, typically covering tuition fees and possibly a living allowance, application deadline "to be announced"; (2) the KNB Scholarship - the Indonesian government scheme for designated developing countries, covering tuition, living allowance, health insurance, settlement allowance and return airfare, with a one-semester Bahasa Indonesia preparatory programme; (3) the Indonesian Aid Scholarship (TIAS) - Ministry of Finance, for future public-sector leaders from partner countries, from associate to master level; and (4) the ASEAN-Maybank Scholarship - undergraduate only and restricted to citizens of the 10 ASEAN member states. No presidential award appears, today or in the earlier (2026-10-25) read of the same page that underlies the surviving record 541. The genuine ITB channels are therefore already in the catalogue: record 541 (Ganesha Talent-International Fellowship) and record 579 (KNB Scholarship). This retired row previously carried an invented 14,000 US dollars and a May 31 annual deadline, both removed in the 2026-10-26 decontamination, after which it sat as an unverified placeholder at reliability 4; it is now closed rather than rewritten. TIAS, visible on the fetched page but not yet in the catalogue, may be evaluated for a future additions batch; its partner-country eligibility was not established here.', requirements = 'Do not apply on the basis of this record - it is retired and names no real award. For ITB as an international student, see record 541 (Ganesha Talent-International Fellowship, ITB-funded for master and doctoral study) and record 579 (KNB Scholarship, the national scheme for designated developing countries, for which ITB is a host university).', deadline = 'Retired - no award of this name exists, so there is no application round. On the fetched ITB page the Ganesha Talent Fellowship and KNB deadlines were both shown as "to be announced"; read the current cycle on the ITB partnership page and in records 541 and 579.', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', application_status = 'closed', recurrence = 'none', expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = '[]', eligible_countries = '["RETIRED - invented importer name; ITB inbound awards are GT-IF (record 541), KNB (579), TIAS and ASEAN-Maybank (see description)"]', funding_type = 'RETIRED - invented importer name; no ITB Presidential Scholarship exists', tuition_coverage = NULL, coverage_type = 'Unspecified', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, travel_allowance = NULL, accommodation = NULL, required_documents = '[]', english_requirements = 'Not applicable - retired record; see records 541 and 579.', website_url = 'https://partnership.itb.ac.id/scholarships/', application_url = 'https://partnership.itb.ac.id/scholarships/', source_url = 'https://partnership.itb.ac.id/scholarships/', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = false, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = 'PASS 124 RETIREMENT 2026-10-28 (Indonesia): invented importer name. First-hand fetches today: ITB Directorate of Partnerships scholarships page (new source 3142, single chunk - inbound lineup is exactly GT-IF, KNB, TIAS and ASEAN-Maybank, with GT-IF and KNB windows both shown as to be announced) and the ITB admission homepage plus international-programme page (programme structure only, no scholarship of this name). The surviving sibling 541 (Ganesha Talent-International Fellowship, rel 7, rewritten 2026-10-25 from the same partnership page) already documents the real ITB-funded graduate fellowship; 579 covers KNB; ASEAN-Maybank is ASEAN-nationals-only undergraduate; TIAS (Indonesian Aid Scholarship, Ministry of Finance, public-sector oriented) is not yet catalogued and is queued as a possible future-additions candidate - its partner-country terms were NOT read in this pass and nothing about Uzbekistan eligibility is asserted. This row''s invented USD 14,000 and May 31 deadline were already removed on 2026-10-26; importer root source 2546 retained as audit trail; new source 3142 also linked to 541 (which had no source links). No university_scholarships row existed; university_id remains NULL (ITB''s universities row 257 is used by 541). Do not revive. Rel 9.' WHERE id = 398;

-- 3) Retire 339 (survivor: 500 UM Bright Scholarship; UM aid hosts unreachable - no new source minted)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Universiti Malaya - ''Bright Sparks and Graduate Fellowship'' welds a long-closed programme (Bright Sparks, est. 2009) to a generic label; UM''s live award is the Bright Scholarship (retired)', description = 'RETIRED in Pass 124 (2026-10-28): this title welds two different things into one award that does not exist. The first half has a real ancestor - UM''s Bright Sparks Program was established on 9 September 2009 by the Institute of Graduate Studies to recruit outstanding full-time PhD candidates - but the Institute''s official scholarship page states that applications for the Bright Sparks Program are closed, and no current call exists; the second half, "Graduate Fellowship", is a generic label, not a UM award name. The instrument UM actually offers international doctoral students today is the UM Bright Scholarship, documented in the surviving record 500 from UM''s official aid page (verified 2026-10-23: full tuition-fee waiver for seven semesters plus MYR 3,500 a month for up to 42 months, for a PhD by research, typically under 30; the same official source states UM offers no undergraduate scholarship to international students). UM''s homepage, fetched for this pass, routes all postgraduate aid to that same official financial-aid page - there is no Bright Sparks application channel in the university''s current structure. National routes into UM also exist outside the university (the Malaysia International Scholarship, record 603; MTCP is listed by the Institute of Graduate Studies). This retired row previously carried an invented 14,000 US dollars and a June 30 annual deadline, both removed in the 2026-10-26 decontamination, after which it sat as an unverified placeholder at reliability 4 pointing at a scholarships sub-address that no longer resolves in the university''s current navigation. It is closed rather than rewritten: the open, appliable UM award is record 500.', requirements = 'Do not apply on the basis of this record - the Bright Sparks Program is closed and the combined name names no open award. For Universiti Malaya''s own funding see record 500 (UM Bright Scholarship, PhD by research), and for the national route see record 603 (Malaysia International Scholarship).', deadline = 'Retired - the Bright Sparks Program is closed and there is no application round under this combined name. The live UM award runs an annual call (see record 500).', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', application_status = 'closed', recurrence = 'none', expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = '[]', eligible_countries = '["RETIRED - welded/dormant name; Bright Sparks applications are closed and UM''s live institutional award is the Bright Scholarship (record 500)"]', funding_type = 'RETIRED - welded name (closed Bright Sparks Program + generic label); see record 500 for UM''s live award', tuition_coverage = NULL, coverage_type = 'Unspecified', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, travel_allowance = NULL, accommodation = NULL, required_documents = '[]', english_requirements = 'Not applicable - retired record; see record 500.', website_url = 'https://aasd.um.edu.my/financial-aid-for-postgraduate', application_url = 'https://aasd.um.edu.my/financial-aid-for-postgraduate', source_url = 'https://aasd.um.edu.my/financial-aid-for-postgraduate', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = false, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = 'PASS 124 RETIREMENT 2026-10-28 (Malaysia): welded/dormant name. Fetch transparency: UM''s aid subdomains (aadc.um.edu.my - the stored address, aasd.um.edu.my and ips.um.edu.my) were unreachable to this project''s fetcher on 2026-10-28 (four failed attempts; one empty response), so no UM aid page was read first-hand in this pass and NO new source row was minted for an unread page. What was fetched first-hand today: um.edu.my homepage (current navigation routes Scholarship & Financial Aid - Postgraduate to aasd.um.edu.my/financial-aid-for-postgraduate, the same aid family as record 500''s verified source) and study.um.edu.my. The disposition rests on (a) record 500''s 2026-10-23 first-hand verification from UM''s official aid page (UM Bright Scholarship is the university''s own international award; no undergraduate international scholarship), and (b) the search-index rendering of the Institute of Graduate Studies official pages, surfaced today: the Bright Sparks Program about page (established 2009-09-09; full-time PhD; scholarship unit contacts) and the IPS scholarship page stating "The application of Bright Sparks Program is closed at this moment" alongside MIS/MTCP/CSFP listings. Snippet content is used here only as audit provenance for a RETIREMENT (the award as named is not open/appliable), not to encode any live terms; the live terms live in 500. If UM''s aid host becomes fetchable in a later cycle, re-read the postgraduate aid page and uplift 500 (whose min_gpa 3.3 / min_ielts 6 and nonstandard award_basis full_tuition are queued hygiene). This row''s invented USD 14,000 and June 30 deadline were already removed on 2026-10-26; importer root source 2652 retained; catalogue row us 584 deleted; university_id 77 retained. Do not revive as a combined name. Rel 9.' WHERE id = 339;

